{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-04-27T20:37:00.421Z","tool_name":"write_file","tool_id":"write_file_1777322220420_1","parameters":{"file_path":"papers/README.md","content":"# Downloaded Papers\n\n1. [AI models collapse when trained on recursively generated data](2305_17493_model_collapse.pdf)\n   - Authors: Ilia Shumailov, Zakhar Shumaylov, Yiren Zhao, Nicolas Papernot, Ross Anderson, Yarin Gal\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: 2305.17493\n   - Why relevant: Foundational paper on model collapse showing that training generative models recursively on their own generated data causes original distribution tails to disappear.\n\n2. [Cooperate or Collapse: Emergence of Sustainable Cooperation in a Society of LLM Agents](2402_04259_cooperate_collapse.pdf)\n   - Authors: Giorgio Piatti, Zhijing Jin, Max Kleiman-Weiner, Bernhard Schölkopf, Mrinmaya Sachan, Rada Mihalcea\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: 2402.04259\n   - Why relevant: Addresses the hypothesis from the perspective of an LLM agent ecosystem managing a common resource. Investigates whether multi-agent systems can achieve sustainable cooperation without collapsing.\n\n3. [Epistemic diversity across language models mitigates knowledge collapse](2407_08480_epistemic_diversity.pdf)\n   - Authors: Damian Hodel, Jevin D. West\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2407.08480\n   - Why relevant: Directly addresses the research hypothesis by investigating if increasing the diversity of models in an AI ecosystem can mitigate collapse.\n\n4. [Data Augmentation using Large Language Models](2402_11894_data_augmentation.pdf)\n   - Authors: Bosheng Ding, et al.\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: 2402.11894\n   - Why relevant: Reviews how LLM-generated data is used for further training and data augmentation, highlighting the challenges of maintaining data diversity and avoiding collapse.\n\n5. [Model Collapse Does Not Mean What You Think](2408_06456_model_collapse_revisited.pdf)\n   - Authors: Rylan Schaeffer, Joshua Kazdan, A. Arulandu, Oluwasanmi Koyejo\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2408.06456\n   - Why relevant: Provides a critical reassessment of the model collapse literature, arguing that different interpretations of model collapse affect future generative models in ways that may be more avoidable in real-world scenarios.\n"}}
